<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#kebek-coin">Glossary</a> · Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kebek (coin)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1320s</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as kebeks</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The kebek was a standardised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coin introduced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kebek-khan">Kebek Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> in the 1320s. It was so widely trusted that it became the basis of later currency in the region. It was part of the most serious attempt to strengthen the khanate's economy and administration.</p></div>
